  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipatory Action in the Asia- Pacific with UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs, World Food Program and Australian Humanitarian Partnership, to support the development of anticipatory interventions for imminent disasters which safeguard lives, livelihoods, and assets - reducing the social and economic impacts of disasters.
&#x200d;
Australia supported Fiji&#x2019;s AA Framework, completed February 2024 and the first of its kind in the Pacific. Innovative climate and weather data to track the risk of an oncoming cyclone. If an agreed parametric trigger is reached, USD $3.778 million of pre-approved financing from the UN will be used to distribute cash, sexual and reproductive health and boat tie down kits and other assistance to vulnerable communities, through agreed partners and Fiji&#x2019;s existing government systems in advance of a cyclone.  
&#x200d;
These interventions will allow communities to act early to protect themselves and their assets, strengthening their disaster and climate resilience.</narrative>
    </description>
